            this relation induces the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            = succeed "-version" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            which is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            (localized at some primes). This maybe deserves to be called
            = succeed "." do
              %em modular equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %p
            This hasn’t been studied much yet (or not at all), but there is some motivation for this from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#MotivationFromStringTheory"} below
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#KrizSati05"} Kriz-Sati 05, p.3, p. 17, 18
          %h3#MotivationFromStringTheory Motivation from string theory
          %p
            A relevant role of some modular equivariant elliptic cohomology theory in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            has been conjectured in (
            %a{:href => "#KrizSati05"}> Kriz-Sati 05, p. 3, p. 17, 18
            ):
          %p
            First of all,
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charges"} D-brane charges
            in general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring+theory"} type II superstring theory
            (hence also of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I+superstring+theory"} type I superstring theory
          %p
            Next, there are various hints (
            %a{:href => "#KrizSati04a"}> Kriz-Sati 04a
            ,
            %a{:href => "#KrizSati04b"} Kriz-Sati 04b
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#KrizSati05"} Kriz-Sati 05
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Sati05"} Sati 05
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            to “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"}> M-theory
            ” involves replacing K-theory by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+orientation+of+tmf"} String orientation of tmf
            (
            %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsStrickland01"}> Ando-Hopkins-Strickland 01
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk10"} Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticle"} superparticle
            (such as that at the end of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            ending on a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+genus"} Todd genus
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU-theory"} KU-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            itself (possibly itself being the boundary of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            ending on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O9+plane"} O9 plane
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"}> heterotic string
            ) or on an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            (self-dual “M-string”)) is given by the refined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            (thus yielding “O9-plane charge” and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane+charge"} M5-brane charge
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sati10"}> Sati 10
            )).
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
