            is (or is naturally identified as)
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axio-dilaton"} axio-dilaton
            of the type II string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            including the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            acting on this as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+fibration"} elliptic fibration
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            (whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monodromy"} monodromy
            “homology invariant” is hence an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+system"} local system
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            = succeed "-equivariance" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            backgrounds which is captured by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
            lifts in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
            to some combined worldsheet/target space
            = succeed "-action." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
            as indicated above (and as realized by theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheEquivariantConstruction"}
            below), and and it is what is conjectured in (
            %a{:href => "#KrizSati05"}> Kriz-Sati 05, p.3
            ) (there the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi SL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z})
            is mentioned, the explicit construction
            %a{:href => "#Definition"} below
            does capture this but also includes equivariance under all other
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z})
          %p
            So by extrapolation from the case of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
            (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+space"}> real space
            ”-structure) is accompanied by a
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet+parity+operator"} worldsheet parity operator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            operations on the target space background would be accompanied by certain modular action on the worldsheet.
          %p
            Mathematically this is precisely what happens in the equivariant version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            established by theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheEquivariantConstruction"}
            below, which by prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SystemOfModuliStacks"}
            has the modular group action on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            induced from the canonical action of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            on moduli of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"} elliptic curves
            (hence:
            = succeed "-1" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheets"} worldsheets
          %p
            Physically such an effect seems not to have been discussed much, but at least the following is knonw: first of all, under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            theory of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+superstring"} type IIB superstring
            certainly is affected: the superstring here is generally a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28p%2Cq%29-string"} (p,q)-string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound state
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            actual fundamental strings (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1-branes"}> F1-branes
            ) with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D1-branes"} D1-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi SL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            does act canonically on these pairs of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+transformation"} conformal transformation
            as the above mathematical story would suggest has been highlighted for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Bandos00"}> Bandos 00
            ).
          %p
            Generally, notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstrings"} type II superstrings
            lands in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence+subgroup"} congruence subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi SL
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_0(2) \hookrightarrow SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            inside the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+group"} modular group
            (see at
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "Witten+genus#ModularityForTypeIISuperstring"} Witten genus – Modularity – For type II superstring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structures"} spin structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            does have a “topological” (homotopy theoretic) lift to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic cohomology
            (as is known for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            via the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} string orientation of tmf
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TMF"} TMF
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi TMF
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
